' 11 Record envelope: the space-owned envelopes of the records of a native space.
'
' Source of Figure N12.8 in ../design.md (section N12). The figure restates
' the module documentation and the encoders of
' rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/record.rs: the version 1 envelopes of
' a datum, a continuation, a counter and a config (decision M-2), the
' priority-queue slots (decision 38), and the version 2 envelope of a join
' continuation (decision 29). It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. Every record starts with a list whose first element is its tag.
'   2. A datum keeps its payload after the envelope, and the host fields of
'      the datum stay outside the envelope.
'   3. A continuation of one bind keeps version 1. A join waiter keeps
'      version 2, with one slot for each position of its canonical group.
'   4. A fire of a join waiter puts its results back into bind order by the
'      bind index of each slot.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 11-record-envelope.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 11-record-envelope
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor $rrs_relation
  RoundCorner 8
}
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
left to right direction
title Space records: the envelopes of version 1 and the join continuation of version 2

rectangle TAG $rrs_tag [
**Record tag:** a GByteArray of four bytes
<latex>\mathit{tag} = [\mathtt{0xE0},\ \mathtt{0x52},\ \mathit{kind},\ \mathit{version}]</latex>
kind: D datum, K continuation, S counter, C config
version 1 for every record, version 2 for a join waiter
]

rectangle DATUM $rrs_storage [
**Datum record, version 1**, on <latex>D(\mathit{sid}, k)</latex>
|= par |= content |
| 0 | <latex>\mathrm{EList}[\mathit{tag}_D,\ \mathrm{GInt}(\mathit{ord}),\ \mathit{priority},\ \mathit{embedding}]</latex> |
| 1 to n | the payload of the send |
The random state, the cost authority and the cost stack
of the send stay outside the envelope.
A priority queue puts the level of the record in its priority slot.
]

rectangle META $rrs_storage [
**Counter and config records, version 1**
|= record |= pars |
| counter on <latex>S(\mathit{sid})</latex> or <latex>S(\mathit{sid}, k)</latex> | <latex>[\mathrm{EList}[\mathit{tag}_S],\ \mathrm{GInt}(n)]</latex> |
| config on <latex>C(\mathit{sid})</latex> | <latex>[\mathrm{EList}[\mathit{tag}_C],\ \mathit{config\ map}]</latex> |
No space datum is a single number (decision M-2).
]

rectangle K1 $rrs_storage [
**Continuation of one bind, version 1**, on <latex>[D(\mathit{sid}, k)]</latex>
<latex>\mathrm{ParBody.body} = \mathrm{Par}\{\mathrm{exprs}: [\mathrm{EList}[\mathit{tag}_K,\ \mathrm{GInt}(\mathit{ord}),\ \mathit{policy},\ \mathit{body}]]\}</latex>
policy: Nil, or the lane of a priority queue
The random state, the guard and the cost authority stay outside.
]

rectangle K2 $rrs_storage [
**Continuation of a join, version 2**, on its canonical group <latex>G = [c_0, \dots, c_{n-1}]</latex>
<latex>\mathrm{ParBody.body} = \mathrm{Par}\{\mathrm{exprs}: [\mathrm{EList}[\mathit{tag}_{K2},\ \mathrm{EList}[s_0, \dots, s_{n-1}],\ \mathit{body}]]\}</latex>
|= slot <latex>s_i</latex> |= content |
| <latex>\mathrm{GInt}(\mathit{ord}_i)</latex> | the order of the waiter in the collection of the position i |
| <latex>\mathrm{GInt}(\mathit{bind}_i)</latex> | the bind of the position i in the receive |
| <latex>\mathit{policy}_i</latex> | Nil, or the lane of a bind on a priority queue |
The bind indices are a permutation of <latex>0, \dots, n-1</latex>.
Repeated channels of one collection have equal orders.
]

rectangle FIRE $rrs_agent [
**A fire of a join waiter**
The receipt gives the results <latex>r_0, \dots, r_{n-1}</latex> in group order.
restore_bind_order puts <latex>r_i</latex> at the bind <latex>\mathit{bind}_i</latex>.
The body then binds its values in the bind order of the receive.
]

TAG --> DATUM : kind D
TAG --> META : kinds S and C
TAG --> K1 : kind K, version 1
TAG --> K2 : kind K, version 2
K2 --> FIRE : the slots

note right of K2
  The decoders of each version compare the whole tag,
  so a version 1 decoder rejects a version 2 record,
  and a version 2 decoder rejects a version 1 record.
  Every decoder is strict: a record that is not the
  exact image of its encoder is Inconsistent.
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_tag>      | the record tag under the namespace byte 0xE0 |
|<$rrs_storage>  | stored records: data, counters, the config and parked continuations |
|<$rrs_agent>    | the outcome of a fire in the space agent |
endlegend
@enduml
